   141	theorem supplies a legitimately finite or uniformly bounded menu of
   142	`(alpha,beta)` types, together with the provenance needed to place every
   143	counterexample in that menu (and with the relevant constants bounded over the
   144	menu). KJN alone does not supply that type theorem. Thus neither KJN nor the
   145	stronger local conjectures, by themselves, makes the whole ladder
