   184	   or the coordinator use `ops/artifact_finalize.py` by default:
   185	   `begin -> close -> finalize -> verify`. Authors write only the leased
   186	   private partial; the tracked read-only manifest accompanies the final
   187	   report. Root verifies after author completion and runs `verify --staged`
   188	   on the explicitly staged report/manifest before commit. This supplements,
   189	   rather than replaces, replay and hostile mathematical review. Existing
   190	   external `ops/lane.sh` custody remains unchanged until a separate adapter
   191	   migration is reviewed; do not retrofit the transaction into a live lane.
   192	
   193	## Promotion and adversarial review
   194	
   195	1. **Different-model promotion.** No result enters `AUDIT.md` as promoted
   196	   until a different model has performed hostile review. Self-review and two
   197	   agents backed by the same producing model do not satisfy this rule.
   198	2. **Recompute, do not defer.** Review the exact source statement, hypotheses,
   199	   transcription, code, certificate, and conclusion as applicable. A second
   200	   prose opinion is not a computational review.
   201	   For a characteristic-`p`, Witt, or `p`-adic successor residual, independently
   202	   reconstruct the integer quotient and compare its generated rows with the
   203	   exact source identity on both a symbolic control and, where possible, an
   204	   old-pass/new-fail negative control. A mod-`p` bracket calculation alone does
   205	   not review a divided carry.
   206	3. **Priority by exposure.** Review priority is proportional to
   207	   `downstream fanout x centrality x fragility x rollback cost`. A claim that
   208	   many active lanes consume outranks an isolated lemma of equal apparent
   209	   importance.
   210	4. **Latency targets.** Start review as soon as a claim becomes provisional.
   211	   Aim to resolve high-fanout claims within six hours and ordinary claims by
   212	   the next full ideation round. A miss is review debt, recorded in `LIVE
   213	   STATE`; it is not silent permission to promote.
   214	5. **Immutable review inputs.**  Give every background reviewer a frozen,
   215	   hash-pinned claim packet (including the exact canonical excerpts it may
   216	   need) and require it to review those bytes.  Do not make a long review
   217	   depend on rereading mutable live ledgers, and do not freeze canonical
   218	   promotion while that review runs.  Later ledger changes are queued for a
   219	   delta review if they alter the charged claim; unrelated drift is not a
   220	   custody failure.
   221	6. **Fail closed.** `REFUTED` triggers immediate rollback. `GAP` preserves only
   222	   the portion actually checked. Corrections are appended promptly to
   223	   `notes.md`, the relevant canonical route/evidence file, and the current
   224	   daily digest.
   225	
   226	When the current reduction architecture is discussed, use the scoped names
   227	`G2-PSC` (global packet/sheet transport and fidelity) and `G2-BD`
   228	(post-residue-A bounded delay), never bare `G2`. The detailed dependency map
   229	is `ladder/REDUCTION.md`; summaries elsewhere must preserve its arrow
   230	directions and scope.
   231	
   232	## Speculative parallelism and rollback
   233	
   234	Review runs in the background. Once a claim is provisional, cheap and
   235	reversible dependent exploration may begin under a visible speculative
   236	budget:
   237	
   238	- at most three child lanes and one unreviewed dependency generation per
   239	  provisional claim;
   240	- at most six active provisional roots campaign-wide;
   241	- normally no more than 25% of active research capacity may depend on any one
   242	  unreviewed claim;
   243	- enqueue hostile review before launching the first dependent child; a missed
   244	  review deadline freezes new descendants but not unrelated work;
   245	- cap each speculative child at six hours unless the coordinator records a
   246	  reasoned exception;
   247	- publication, promotion, irreversible action, expensive fleet campaigns, and
   248	  further fanout must not rely on an unreviewed claim;
   249	- every dependent report labels the assumption `PROVISIONAL`, so descendants
   250	  can be found and rolled back mechanically.
   251	
   252	The coordinator maintains a lightweight claim DAG in the newest `LIVE STATE`
   253	block: claim ID, exact scope, evidence tier, lifecycle, parents, owner,
   254	reviewer, artifact hashes, descendants, and stop condition. If a premise is
   255	refuted or narrowed, quarantine its descendants immediately, retain them as
   256	conditional work when useful, and re-root any result whose proof did not
   257	actually need the failed premise.
   258	
   259	For each load-bearing bridge, prefer three concurrent attacks when useful and
   260	affordable: prove it, falsify it on the cheapest honest model, and bypass it by
   261	redesigning the route. A negative result closes only its registered scope.
   262	
   263	## The continuous outer loop
   264	
   265	Cadences below are maximum quiet intervals, never reasons to wait. Any event
   266	may interrupt the current allocation; unrelated work continues.
   267	
   268	### Event triggers and micro-rounds
   269	
   270	Run an immediate strategy update when any of these occurs:
   271	
   272	- a decisive lane confirms, refutes, gaps, caps, or times out;
   273	- a new mathematical object, theorem, countermodel, certificate, or materially
   274	  faster instrument is banked;
   275	- review changes a claim's scope or lifecycle;
   276	- an external result or actor changes correctness, route rank, priority,
   277	  publication posture, available artifacts, or competitive status;
   278	- the active portfolio is stalled, duplicated, or exposed to one fragile
   279	  premise beyond the limits above;
   280	- campaign machinery loses or delays state, duplicates work, misroutes a
   281	  model or compute job, exposes mutable inputs, materially inflates context or
   282	  cost, or reports fleet/lane state unreliably.  Treat this as a bounded
   283	  systems micro-round unless it also changes the mathematical ranking.
   284	
   285	A targeted response to a routine local event is a **micro-round**: triage the
   286	delta, launch or stop bounded work, and bank it without forcing every ideator
   287	to rescan all avenues. It does not reset the 12-hour clock. A credible external
   288	proof/counterexample, a load-bearing review reversal, or a new result changing
   289	the global ranking or critical-path hypotheses is critical and starts a full
   290	round immediately, subject to the coalescing rule below. A new promoted entry
   291	alone does not force a whole-portfolio rescan. Other events start a full round when they
   292	materially change the global ranking; otherwise they receive a micro-round.
   293	
   294	The September6 12:55Z48-hour trial ended September8 12:55Z. The September8
   295	2220 synthesis continues its scoped-event rule: routine scoped lemmas and
   296	instrument instantiations receive targeted review plus the theorem-interface
   297	composition pass, not an automatic full scan solely because promotion is new.
   298	Observed benefit includes15i's avoided identical echo scan; no controlled
   299	throughput estimate or complete avoided-scan census is claimed. The missed
   300	trial checkpoint and interruption/cadence debt remain recorded in notes.
   301	This changes no hostile-review gate, critical scope-reversal response, or
   302	12-hour completed-round backstop. Track avoided duplication, integration
   303	time and review latency with existing records; revert if important cross-route
   304	consequences are missed. Record the ranking/critical-path assessment for
   305	each micro-round. Prepare invitations while root writes its blind, but do
   306	not invite before root's seal or retroactively reset a frozen deadline.
   307	
   308	Coalesce echo events to prevent review/round thrashing. If a sealed full-round
   309	packet already states a provisional result's complete mathematical content and
   310	the post-cutoff review merely confirms that same content and scope, harvest the
   311	lifecycle promotion as a micro-round; it does not trigger an otherwise
   312	identical full scan. A refutation or scope change of a **promoted or
   313	load-bearing** claim, a new dependency on the critical path, or a materially
   314	rank-changing review fact remains a critical trigger. An expected negative
   315	first-gate result or correction to an unpromoted provisional formula may be
   316	coalesced when the global ranking and trust perimeter are unchanged. Record
   317	the coalescing decision explicitly in the next synthesis or `LIVE STATE`.
   318	
   319	Every new provisional or promoted theorem also triggers a **theorem-interface
   320	composition pass**.  Normalize it to object, hypotheses, field/ring, degree or
   321	support bounds, and conclusion; search the claim DAG for results whose
   322	conclusions discharge those hypotheses or whose hypotheses consume the new
   323	conclusion; and test the cheapest exact pairings before treating the theorem
   324	as an isolated endpoint.  Record a new bridge, a scope mismatch, or `NO HIT`.
   325	This pass is bounded and does not interrupt unrelated work.  In particular,
   326	compare proof-side degree/automorphy theorems with counterexample-side
   327	integrality, specialization, compactness, and collision lemmas: their labels
   328	may differ even when their theorem interfaces compose.
   329	
   330	If a critical event arrives during an open full round and invalidates a
   331	load-bearing snapshot assumption, mark that round `ABORTED` and reseal. If it
   332	does not invalidate the packet, take any safe emergency action, finish the
   333	sealed round, and start an immediate follow-on full round. Never mutate the
   334	open snapshot in place.
   335	
   336	### Full-spectrum ideation — at least every 12 hours
   337	
   338	No more than 12 hours may pass between completed full rounds. A significant
   339	event starts one sooner. Each round follows this protocol:
   340	
   341	1. **Freeze a state packet.** Record UTC time, clean basis commit, newer local
   342	   hashes if any, newest `LIVE STATE`, active/recent lane reports, review debt,
   343	   current `APPROACHES.md`, load-bearing `AUDIT.md` corrections, and all new
   344	   external evidence since the prior round.
   345	2. **Blind independent scan.** Every active research agent is a core ideator by
   346	   default and reads the whole avenue map, current gaps, and new evidence
   347	   before seeing the other submissions. A noninterruptible compute or review
   348	   worker may be omitted explicitly; mark the round degraded if this leaves
   349	   inadequate coverage. A rotating specialist lens may be added only after
   350	   the common scan. Model diversity is preferred; duplicate instances still
   351	   think independently.
   352	   After the September6 1210Z round, the automatic whole-portfolio roster is
   353	   Astra, Fable, and Sol. Opus and Grok are bounded utility seats and may be
   354	   invited for a concrete additional lens. Current1210Z invitations remain.
   355	   Whole-portfolio models are invited automatically. Each receives the
   356	   same sealed packet, submission contract, tool boundary, and deadline, and
   357	   must submit before seeing any other lane's report.  Every submission
   358	   receives equal post-deduplication consideration: model identity is neither
   359	   a bonus nor a vote, and operational unavailability degrades but does not
   360	   block the round.
   361	3. **Required submission contract.** Each report gives:
   362	   - a compact disposition vector over every numbered avenue: `unchanged`,
   363	     `raise`, `lower`, or `reopen`, with reasons for every change;
   364	   - a reranking of the principal proof and disproof bottlenecks;
   365	   - one genuinely new mechanism, or an explicit `NO_NEW_MECHANISM` with
   366	     evidence that the best use of capacity is an existing unresolved target;
   367	   - at least one new connection between existing avenues;
   368	   - the strongest proof attack and strongest counterexample/falsification
   369	     attack;
   370	   - one software acceleration or decisive experiment;
   371	   - a short campaign-systems check, independent of the mathematical software
   372	     proposal: either an `UPGRADE` card with the smallest useful test or
   373	     implementation, or `NO_CHANGE` with evidence.  Rotate across state
   374	     freshness, context and retrieval cost, claim/review propagation,
   375	     duplication, model routing and utilization, adapter reliability, AWS
   376	     scheduling and cost, reproducibility, and operator/chat-summary quality;
   377	   - no more than three detailed idea cards, each with explicit dependencies,
   378	     cheapest discriminator, interpretation of each outcome, stop condition,
   379	     and expected information gain;
   380	   - a `continue / redesign / stop` recommendation for current major lanes.
   381	4. **Deduplicate after collection.** Fingerprint ideas by target obstruction,
   382	   mechanism, object, and decisive test. Merge operational duplicates while
   383	   preserving independent origins, disagreements, and genuinely different proof
   384	   mechanisms. Shared wording is not independent support.
   385	5. **Cross-pollinate adversarially.** Only after blind collection, ask lanes to
   386	   combine compatible ideas, expose shared hidden assumptions, attack the
   387	   strongest proposal, and design the cheapest experiment that separates the
   388	   leading choices.
   389	6. **Run the canonical history/priority checksum.** Before compute, search
   390	   `AUDIT.md`, `APPROACHES.md`, `PROGRESS.md`, the newest `LIVE STATE`,
   391	   `ladder/REDUCTION.md`, and repository reports for every surviving target,
   392	   mechanism, and close synonym. Reconcile the master known-degree/closed-case
   393	   ledgers, then check each load-bearing literature claim in primary text.
   394	   Label every card `NEW`, `KNOWN`, `DUPLICATE`, or `SCOPE-CONFLICT` in the
   395	   synthesis. Blind consensus never overrides a banked exact result or primary
   396	   theorem; a shared stale packet premise is correlated error, not a vote.
   397	7. **Synthesize and launch.** The coordinator writes a ranked synthesis,
   398	   updates the avenue/claim graphs if needed, assigns owners and reviewers,
   399	   launches reversible lanes immediately, and records why alternatives were
   400	   deferred or stopped.  Deduplicate the systems checks, choose at most one
   401	   highest-value bounded upgrade for immediate work, and track it only in the
   402	   canonical `LIVE STATE` queue.  Trial at least one incremental machinery
   403	   improvement in every rolling 48-hour window unless no candidate clears its
   404	   measured benefit, regression-risk, and mathematical-opportunity-cost gate;
   405	   record a reasoned `NO_UPGRADE` rather than changing machinery for its own
   406	   sake.  Systems work runs beside, and normally does not block, live
   407	   mathematical research.
   408	
   409	Target 60 minutes for blind submissions, 30 for cross-pollination, and 30 for
   410	synthesis. Close a round within two hours when possible; if an ideator misses
   411	the close, mark the round `DEGRADED` instead of blocking ongoing research.
   412	Events arriving after the snapshot are queued for the next micro/full round
   413	and never silently mutate the sealed packet.
   414	
   415	Round artifacts use
   416	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-<lane>.md` and
   417	`xmodel/ideation-<YYYYMMDDTHHMMZ>-synthesis.md`.
   418	
   419	### External web sweep — at least every 24 hours
   420	
   421	No more than 24 hours may pass between completed broad sweeps. Low-cost alerts
   422	and known-actor watches run between sweeps when available. An external event
   423	can trigger both immediate intake and a full ideation round.
   424	
   425	The sweep covers broad phrase/concept searches as well as arXiv, repositories,
   426	Zenodo, MathOverflow, Palomar and its public discussion channels, relevant
   427	social feeds, citations, and the known-actor watchlist. Date-windowed searches
   428	are supplemental, because old but newly discovered artifacts have already
   429	escaped them.
   430	
   431	Classify an item `ACTIONABLE` only if it can change correctness, route rank,
   432	priority/publication posture, artifacts, or actor status. For each actionable
   433	item: preserve URL and timestamp, snapshot or hash the artifact, extract the
   434	exact claim without overreading it, replay the cheapest decisive check, map it
   435	to the claim DAG and avenue graph, and assign follow-up. Bank a negative sweep
   436	too; absence of a hit is weak evidence, not evidence of absence.
   437	
   438	### Classical frontier admissibility gate
   439	
   440	Before registering compute, every lane must state separately the actual total
   441	degrees, partial-`y` degrees, weighted degrees, and whether any total/
   442	coefficient-`x` cap is finite.  It must then reconcile that honest scope with
   443	the classical closed-case ledger and primary sources.  In particular, the
   444	Guccione--Guccione--Valqui/Heitmann theorem requires
   445	`gcd(deg_total P,deg_total Q) >= 16` for a characteristic-zero
   446	counterexample.  Thus every envelope with both total degrees at most `12`
   447	and every explicitly registered fixed actual-total pair such as `(9,12)` or
   448	`(8,12)` is counterexample-closed.  Historical `max12` and “maximum-12” tags
   449	normally name a maximum actual partial-`y`-degree frontier; they never
   450	establish a finite coefficient-`x` or total-degree cap.  Only an explicit
   451	actual-total pair or total cap licenses `METHOD_CONTROL_ONLY`; an unbounded-
   452	total partial-`y` lane remains `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` unless another
   453	theorem closes its exact scope.
   454	
   455	For the mechanically covered cases, attach the deterministic output of
   456	`ops/frontier_gate.py` to `REGISTRATION.md`.  A
   457	`REFUSE_CLASSICALLY_CLOSED` verdict blocks frontier compute.  Such a lane may
   458	run only after being relabelled `method-control`, with a named live client and
   459	a strict cost/stop condition; its output cannot be advertised as advancing
   460	the closed degree frontier.  `NOT_CLOSED_BY_THIS_GATE` means only that this
   461	one theorem is inconclusive.  Unbounded-total partial-`y` work must say
   462	`--total-unbounded` explicitly and still pass every other classical/history
   463	check.  Any significant routing news reruns this gate across active lanes
   464	before further capacity is allocated.
   465	
   466	**External maximum-degree overlay (September6 12:42Z).** In addition to the
   467	gcd theorem, GGHV arXiv:2204.14178v1 excludes characteristic-zero polynomial
   468	Keller counterexamples with actual maximum total degree below108. Primary
   469	applicability is recorded in AUDIT17(jjjjjjjjjjjj), with imported reduction
   470	dependencies remaining externally trusted. Thus actual99/66 is closed despite
   471	passing the gcd screen. Do not turn the paper's normalized sub125 pair list
   472	into an arbitrary-representative filter, or apply this bound to partial-y
   473	degrees with unbounded total degree or to Laurent/J=x^k charts. The installed
   474	overlay has passed the scoped different-model Astra review of Sol's code
   475	(xmodel/frontier-external108-root-gate-astra-20260906.md);
   476	its legacy verdict remains gcd-only and overall_verdict combines both bounds.
   477	The manual external check remains mandatory for actual source-degree
   478	declarations and literature beyond the implemented bounds.
   479	An inconclusive tool verdict never
   480	certifies openness against unimplemented theorems. No frontier rerun of99
   481	is authorized; a method control needs a named client and strict stop condition.
   482	
   483	## Capacity allocation
   484	
   485	Default portfolio targets, adjusted when evidence demands it:
   486	
   487	- 45% strongest current critical paths;
   488	- 25% new avenues and cross-avenue connections;
   489	- 12% adversarial review and replication; the promotion gate is never queued
   490	  behind frontier work;
   491	- 10% software, instruments, and bounded campaign-system improvement;
   492	- 4% external intelligence;
   493	- 4% state integration.
   494	
   495	These are the September 2 resolution-first defaults, superseding the older
   496	35/20/20/15/5/5 allocation. Formalization remains non-blocking and outside the
   497	separate repository's inspection boundary.
   498	
   499	With four reasoning slots, the usual shape is: coordinator/integrator;
   500	strongest current route; orthogonal new or disproof route; and
   501	risk-prioritized review/rapid response. Use wider model fleets for blind idea
   502	generation and independent review, and separate compute capacity from scarce
   503	reasoning slots. Do not leave all slots exploring descendants of one premise.
   504	
   505	Whenever provisional review debt exists, reserve at least one reasoning slot
   506	or 25% of research capacity (whichever is practical) for review and
   507	falsification. Two consecutive non-informative attempts on the same
   508	representation force a redesign; a third requires written justification. Two
   509	full rounds with unchanged leading gaps and no information gain trigger a
   510	zero-base fresh-eyes reset for one cycle.
   511	
   512	Choose work by expected information gain per unit time and cost, not by how
   513	many agents or tokens it consumes. Track event-to-decisive-test time, review
   514	latency/debt, central gaps resolved, provisional exposure and rollback cost,
   515	new connections actually tested, and information gained per compute dollar.
   516	For campaign machinery also track report-to-ingestion latency, stale or
   517	missing state, context bytes per lane, duplicate work prevented, adapter and
   518	job failure rates, model/fleet utilization, and time to a sealed replayable
   519	certificate.  Retain an upgrade only when those measurements or mathematical
   520	throughput improve without an offsetting reliability regression.
   521	
   522	## Tick, banking, and live state
   523	
   524	At each coordinator tick:
   525	
   526	1. read the newest `LIVE STATE` and any events since it;
   527	2. sweep local lanes and remote machines; verify exact process identities and
   528	   stop idle paid capacity within standing authority;
   529	3. rerun the classical frontier gate on new scopes or significant news;
   530	4. harvest finished work, apply the provisional gate, and start hostile review
   531	   immediately for promotable claims;
   532	5. propagate review outcomes through the claim DAG without blocking unrelated
   533	   work;
   534	6. test the 12-hour ideation and 24-hour sweep deadlines and all event triggers;
   535	7. rebalance the portfolio, launch the next bounded lanes, and assign a stop
   536	   condition to each;
   537	8. append findings, corrections, dead ends, costs, and decisions to `notes.md`,
   538	   then append a fresh `LIVE STATE` block.
   539	
   540	September6 resumption rule (1435 round's collection-delay micro-round):
   541	check overdue terminal collection and exact process/cap obligations before
   542	starting new exploratory work. A wall-clock target is not an assistant-wake
   543	guarantee: keep detached job caps independent of coordinator presence, bank
   544	the actual next collection owner, and report missed checks without resetting
   545	clocks. Use the existing LIVE STATE queue; no second scheduler/ledger is implied.
   546	
   547	Before launch, check active tags, prior `xmodel/` reports, `AUDIT.md`, and
   548	`APPROACHES.md`. One question/deliverable has one live owner unless a second
   549	lane is explicitly registered as independent replication.
   550	
   551	Use this compact block; append rather than editing an old one:
   552	
   553	```text
   554	## <UTC timestamp> LIVE STATE
   555	- Basis: <commit and any explicitly dirty artifact hashes>
   556	- Coordinator / ideators: <active coordinator; full-round research roster>
   557	- Last full ideation: <UTC / round ID>; next deadline: <UTC>
   558	- Last broad web sweep: <UTC / report>; next deadline: <UTC>
   559	- Last system improvement/check: <UTC / result>; next 48-hour checkpoint: <UTC>
   560	- Active lanes: <tag, owner, inputs, stop condition>
   561	- Provisional claims: <ID, tier, parents, descendants, review>
   562	- Review queue/debt: <priority and due time>
   563	- Holds/human gates: <exact action and authority needed>
   564	- Top gaps: <links into APPROACHES/REDUCTION/AUDIT>
   565	- Immediate queue/triggers: <ranked bounded actions>
   566	```
   567	
   568	At the end of a calendar day, update that day's single `PROGRESS.md` entry.
   569	Negative results and superseded plans remain in `notes.md`; they prevent the
   570	campaign from paying twice for the same failed idea.
   571	
   572	## Replayability and operational safety
   573	
   574	- Computational claims ship engines, certificates, exact replay commands,
   575	  versions, input hashes, seeds, host, UTC times, and meaningful negative
   576	  controls. Mod-p work records every prime.
   577	- Exact mathematical integers/rationals cross orchestration as raw bytes or
   578	  decimal strings, never through JavaScript native-number JSON roundtrips.
   579	  Recheck retained values against exact computations, not just file hashes or
   580	  no-float types; a rounded integer can also be wrong. This repairs the specific
   581	  September6 B-witness export failure (AUDIT17(ppppppppppppp)), not a claim that
   582	  all historical artifacts have been audited. Preserve erroneous frozen bytes
   583	  with an explicit erratum and a separately pinned replacement.
   584	- A claimed `python -O` or `-OO` verification is admissible only when every
   585	  load-bearing check remains live in that mode. Freeze an AST scan showing no
   586	  `Assert` nodes in the verification paths (or prove that any remaining
   587	  asserts are non-gating diagnostics), and run a deliberate old-pass/new-fail
   588	  mutation under every claimed interpreter mode. Byte-identical positive
   589	  output alone is insufficient: stripped checks can print the same answer
   590	  vacuously. Ordinary-only scripts may use `assert` only when the report labels
   591	  that limitation and makes no optimized-mode evidence claim.
   592	- A successor residual at digit `n` is typed only after an exact numerator `N`
   593	  is proved divisible by `p^n` on the charged predecessor scheme and
   594	  `N/p^n mod p` is derived with all lower-order divided carries retained. If
   595	  the quotient is not integral on that scheme, or generated coefficient rows
   596	  disagree with an exact determinant/source-identity reconstruction, the gate
   597	  is `TYPE-FAIL` and must not be used downstream.
   598	- msolve 0.10.1 characteristic-zero `-g` may return a first-machine-prime
   599	  unit basis before rational reconstruction while printing a characteristic-0
   600	  header. A char-0-header `[1]` is only first-prime trace evidence unless an
   601	  independently checked exact rational certificate is present. See `AUDIT.md`.
   602	- Run all heavy or uncertain-duration campaign computation on AWS, never on
   603	  the local machine. This includes CAS/solver jobs, Lean builds, and long or
   604	  potentially multi-GB exact-Python replays/enumerations. Reserve local
   605	  execution for editing, orchestration, hashing, status checks, model-review
   606	  adapters without compute tools, and genuinely short low-memory validation.
   607	  Follow `ops/FLEET.md` for machine inventory, shipping, caps, telemetry, and
   608	  kill safety.
   609	- `jc2-lean` is a separately owned nested repository and is outside the
   610	  campaign's inspection boundary. Campaign agents must not enter, enumerate,
   611	  search, read, build, status, modify, or control it. Scope every parent Git
   612	  query explicitly away from that path; never stage its gitlink. The parent
   613	  `.ignore` excludes it from ripgrep-style broad searches. Concurrent local
   614	  formalization may consume shared CPU/RAM, but campaign contention checks
   615	  remain system-level and must not identify or inspect that nested workload.
   616	- New heavy runners fail closed off AWS before importing a CAS or allocating
   617	  large objects, require a registered AWS job tag, and record the remote
   618	  hostname in custody.  New counterexample/frontier runners also record the
   619	  classical admissibility verdict described above before launch.  A
   620	  coordinator process-tree/swap-delta audit
   621	  is part of each live-state checkpoint; allocated swap without new pageouts
   622	  is historical occupancy, not by itself active thrashing.
   623	- A process-group guard is valid only if its recorded group includes the
   624	  actual CAS and every descendant whose RSS or lifetime it must control.
   625	  Wrappers that create an unrecorded inner PGID (including GNU `timeout`
   626	  without `--foreground`) are forbidden unless every inner group is itself
   627	  recorded and validated.  Before a new or repaired heavy runner launches,
   628	  a live no-CAS dummy regression must show that descendant RSS is included in
   629	  telemetry and that namespace-validated TERM, then KILL if needed, leaves no
   630	  nonzombie descendant or orphan; freeze that regression with the source.
   631	- Reviewed `ops/run_capped.py` is the opt-in `CAPRUN/v1` pilot for bounded
   632	  argv-only process groups. Its exact-PGID scope, inherited per-process CPU
   633	  limit, sampled RSS overshoot, and typed incomplete-cleanup outcome are
